  data:  # cc93
    kind: work_item  # cc93
    title: "Go marshal callbacks Phase 2/3: caller-site detection + synthetic dispatches_to edges"  # cc93
    status: todo_soft  # cc93
    priority: 3  # cc93
    parent: WI-pimig-zopuv-tomam-masan-zodub-tifuj-domon-palog  # cc93
    tags:  # cc93
    - linker_gap  # cc93
    - go_analyzer  # cc93
    - serialization_boundary  # cc93
    - cross_language_linkers  # cc93
    isbefore: []  # cc93
    duplicate_of: []  # cc93
    not_duplicate_of: []  # cc93
    pr_ref:  # cc93
    description: "Follow-up to WI-pimig Phase 1 (PR #2942), which validated as fully effective: all 92 marshal methods in alertmanager dead-code candidates were eliminated by classifying serialization_callback methods as LIBRARY_EXPORT entrypoints. Phase 1 solved the dead-code false-positive goal (the original motivation), so Phase 2/3 are about improving call-graph precision rather than fixing a regression.\n\nPHASE 2 (caller-site type detection):\n- Detect call sites of yaml.Unmarshal(b, &v), json.Marshal(v), yaml.NewDecoder(r).Decode(&v).\n- Detect struct fields tagged `yaml:\"...\"` or `json:\"...\"` (transitively, through Config-style types).\n- Build a type->[call_sites] map for each receiver type that implements one of the 8 marshal/unmarshal interfaces.\n\nPHASE 3 (synthetic edges):\n- Emit dispatches_to edges from marshal call sites to the corresponding method definitions.\n- Alternatively, emit synthetic framework_hook or serialization_entry edges from the type's primary caller.\n\nPRIORITY RATIONALE (P3, not P2):\n- The dead-code false-positive elimination motivation is fully addressed by Phase 1.\n- Phase 2/3 would improve slice/reverse-slice precision in YAML/JSON-config-heavy Go projects (alertmanager, prometheus, loki, tempo) by connecting the marshal methods into the live call graph.\n- Without Phase 2/3, marshal methods are still classified as LIBRARY_EXPORT entrypoints (correct), but slices through the type graph won't show the data flow from yaml.Unmarshal -> Config.UnmarshalYAML -> field initialization.\n- This is a quality/precision improvement, not a correctness fix. Schedule when slice quality work resurfaces (DEEP-mode priority #3-4).\n\nREGRESSION TEST: After Phase 2/3 lands, slicing from main() in alertmanager should reach the marshal methods through dispatches_to/serialization_entry edges. Reverse-slice from Config.UnmarshalYAML should identify yaml.Unmarshal call sites as callers.\n\nDEPENDENCIES: Phase 1 (WI-pimig) — done. May benefit from caller-site tracking infrastructure used by other linkers (e.g., grpc, http_calls) — investigate during implementation.\n\nEXTENSION: Equivalent patterns in Java (Jackson @JsonCreator), Python (pydantic validators), C# (IXmlSerializable), TypeScript (class-transformer @Type) — file separate items if Go Phase 2/3 validates the approach."  # cc93
    fields: {}  # cc93
